UPDATE questions SET
  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (D): Under IRC Sections 1361-1379, an S corporation provides pass-through taxation (avoiding double taxation), limited liability protection, and the ability to split income between reasonable salary (subject to FICA) and distributions (not subject to self-employment tax). At $400,000, this splitting significantly reduces total employment taxes.
Wrong (A): A sole proprietorship exposes all net income to self-employment tax and provides no personal liability protection, failing two of Kowalski''s four objectives.
Wrong (B): A general partnership requires at least two partners and offers no liability protection, making it unsuitable for a solo practitioner seeking limited liability.
Wrong (C): A C corporation subjects income to double taxation (corporate and dividend level) and does not allow salary/distribution splitting to reduce self-employment tax.$EXPL$
