Wrong (B): Chapter 7 does not protect all personal property; only assets falling within specific exemption categories and dollar limits are retained by the debtor.
Wrong (C): There is no blanket priority for real property over personal property in bankruptcy; each asset is evaluated against its applicable exemption independently.
