-- Q11250: Debtor-Creditor Relationships [easy/L1]
-- Issues: #3
UPDATE questions SET
  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (A): Under Section 303(b) of the Bankruptcy Code, when a debtor has 12 or more creditors, at least three creditors with aggregate noncontingent, undisputed unsecured claims meeting the statutory threshold must join the involuntary petition. With 18 creditors, this three-creditor minimum applies.
Wrong (B): A single creditor may file only when the debtor has fewer than 12 creditors; with 18 creditors, the three-petitioner rule applies.
Wrong (C): The Code specifies a minimum number of petitioning creditors with qualifying claims, not a majority of all creditors.
Wrong (D): Any single creditor with an undisputed claim is insufficient when the debtor has 12 or more creditors; three must join.$EXPL$
