-- Q11251: Debtor-Creditor Relationships [hard/L4]
-- Issues: #3
UPDATE questions SET
  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (B): Under Section 1129(b) of the Bankruptcy Code, a court may confirm a plan over a dissenting class''s objection (cramdown) only if the plan is fair and equitable and does not discriminate unfairly. For unsecured creditors, fair and equitable means no junior class receives anything unless the dissenting class is paid in full.
Wrong (A): Whether all creditors voted within the statutory period is a procedural matter unrelated to the substantive cramdown standard under Section 1129(b).
Wrong (C): Requiring full payment within 90 days confuses cramdown with administrative expense priority rules; cramdown requires fairness, not a specific payment timeline.
Wrong (D): Cramdown does not require consent from any member of the dissenting class; its purpose is to confirm the plan despite the class''s unanimous rejection.$EXPL$
