  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (C): Under UCC Section 9-502, a financing statement must include the debtor''s name, the secured party''s name, and a description of the collateral. Section 9-506(b) provides that a filing omitting the debtor''s name is seriously misleading and ineffective for perfection.
Wrong (A): A financing statement missing required content is not merely lower priority; it fails entirely to perfect the security interest under Article 9.
Wrong (B): There is no 90-day grace period for correcting a fatally deficient financing statement; the omission renders the filing ineffective from the start.
