  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (C): Under Section 1325(a)(4) of the Bankruptcy Code, a Chapter 13 plan must satisfy the best interests test, requiring that each unsecured creditor receive at least as much as it would in a Chapter 7 liquidation. The proposed 25 cents per dollar is less than the 40 cents available in Chapter 7, so the court must deny confirmation.
Wrong (A): Chapter 13 debtors cannot set repayment below the Chapter 7 liquidation value; the best interests test imposes a floor on distributions to unsecured creditors.
