-- Q11256: Debtor-Creditor Relationships [medium/L2]
-- Issues: #3
UPDATE questions SET
  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (B): Under UCC Section 9-515(a), a financing statement is effective for five years from the date of filing. A continuation statement must be filed within six months before expiration to maintain effectiveness. Filed March 15, 2021, the statement lapsed on March 15, 2026, leaving the security interest unperfected.
Wrong (A): A financing statement does not remain effective indefinitely; UCC Article 9 imposes a five-year limit that requires renewal through a continuation statement.
Wrong (C): The UCC specifies a five-year effectiveness period, not three years; expiration on March 15, 2024 misstates the statutory duration.
