  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (D): Under the Restatement (Third) of Suretyship and Guaranty Section 15, a guarantor of collection has secondary liability, meaning the creditor must first exhaust remedies against the principal debtor before demanding payment from the guarantor. Central Bank sued Nakamura without first pursuing Patel.
Wrong (A): There is no 90-day waiting period for guarantor liability; the distinction depends on whether the guaranty is of payment or of collection, not on time elapsed.
Wrong (B): A guaranty made as part of the same transaction as the underlying loan is supported by that loan''s consideration; separate consideration is not required.
