-- Q11258: Debtor-Creditor Relationships [easy/L1]
-- Issues: #3
UPDATE questions SET
  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (B): Under Section 1101(1) of the Bankruptcy Code, a debtor-in-possession (DIP) is the debtor who continues to operate the business during Chapter 11 reorganization. The DIP has the same powers and duties as a trustee, including authority to use, sell, or lease property of the estate.
Wrong (A): A creditor appointed to manage the debtor''s property describes a receiver, not a debtor-in-possession; the DIP is the debtor itself.
Wrong (C): A trustee who liquidates nonexempt assets describes the Chapter 7 trustee role, not the debtor-in-possession concept unique to Chapter 11.
Wrong (D): A secured creditor holding collateral describes a lienholder''s position, not the debtor-in-possession who retains operational control.$EXPL$
