  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (A): Under Section 362(d)(2) of the Bankruptcy Code, a court shall grant relief from the automatic stay if the debtor has no equity in the property and the property is not necessary for an effective reorganization. The $220,000 mortgage exceeds the $180,000 value, and in Chapter 7 there is no reorganization plan.
Wrong (B): Section 362(d)(2) does not require a showing of irreparable harm within 60 days; the test is lack of equity plus lack of necessity for reorganization.
Wrong (C): The automatic stay can be lifted before discharge under Section 362(d) when the statutory grounds are met; it does not remain in effect regardless of circumstances.
Wrong (D): Section 362(d) applies in all bankruptcy chapters, including Chapter 7, not only in Chapter 11 reorganization proceedings.$EXPL$
