-- Q11261: Debtor-Creditor Relationships [medium/L2]
-- Issues: #3
UPDATE questions SET
  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (D): Under the Restatement (Third) of Suretyship and Guaranty Section 41, a material modification of the underlying obligation without the surety''s consent discharges the surety to the extent of any resulting prejudice. Extending the term and increasing the interest rate are material changes that increase the surety''s risk exposure.
Wrong (A): Material modification without consent is a well-established surety defense; sureties are not bound by changes they did not agree to when those changes increase their risk.
Wrong (B): The surety''s obligation is measured by the original terms, not the modified ones; the higher interest rate cannot be imposed on a non-consenting surety.
Wrong (C): The burden is not on the creditor to prove the modification was harmless; the surety is discharged to the extent of prejudice caused by the unauthorized modification.$EXPL$
WHERE id = 11261;

