UPDATE questions SET
  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (B): Under Section 541(a)(1) of the Bankruptcy Code, property of the estate includes all legal and equitable interests of the debtor in property as of the commencement of the case. This encompasses real and personal property, tangible and intangible assets, and causes of action.
Wrong (A): Property of the estate is determined as of the petition date, not after it; post-petition acquisitions are included only under limited exceptions in Section 541(a)(5).
Wrong (C): The estate is not limited to real property; it includes all legal and equitable interests in any type of property held by the debtor at filing.
