-- Q11264: Debtor-Creditor Relationships [hard/L4]
-- Issues: #3
UPDATE questions SET
  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (D): Under UCC Section 9-317(a)(2), a lien creditor has priority over a security interest that is unperfected at the time the lien arises. Apex''s interest attached May 1 but was not perfected until May 20, while the judicial lien arose May 15 when Apex was still unperfected. The judgment creditor prevails.
Wrong (A): Attachment alone does not establish priority over a lien creditor; the security interest must be perfected before the lien arises to have priority.
Wrong (B): The 20-day retroactive priority under Section 9-324(a) applies only to purchase money security interests, not ordinary security interests like Apex''s loan.
Wrong (C): UCC Article 9 does not recognize equal priority between competing interests; the first-to-perfect or first-to-file rule and lien creditor rules establish a clear hierarchy.$EXPL$
WHERE id = 11264;
